 that has a a um a staff and  a Globus you know and so it  it doesn't always refer exactly to the  same particulars but the structure is  there that you can recognize being  repeated over and over  so you can understand in the manner in  which it would happen there would be  different  ways that it would be played out in the  world this relationship between between  Authority and power between the right  hand and the left hand uh sometimes it  would it could be fractal like even down  at the you can notice how fractal it is  if you look at the keys here for example  and so again Saint Peter for example  hold the keys but you can understand  that one of those keys is on the right  hand and one of those keys is on the  left hand they kind of cross over  because one is to bind and one is to  unbind one is to tighten in the center  and one is to loosen so you can  understand that it's it happened  fractally so even on the right you have  it can be repeated at different levels  where you have again the same symbolism  which is repeated so that's important to  understand because sometimes if you  don't understand that it's fractal it  can become confusing because you're like  okay well then why so if left is  something like unbinding pushing away  like Saint Christ says about the goats  and and uh right is something like  binding or bringing in so then why does  Saint Peter have the two Keys went to a  lock and went to unlock went to bind and  went to unbind and so it has to do with  that and so you could say that Saint  Peter as a stand-in for the center has a  left and a right hand himself and can  manifest that at a lower level  um so that's just a little hint to  understand that as well and so this can  play out in different ways so for  example in the the in the Middle Ages of  course Charlemagne for example was was  crowned by the uh by the pope and and in  the but there's always like a test if  the if the two sides don't get along  together the two sides can fight 